#!/usr/bin/env autodq
# %% [markdown] AutoDQ workspace isolation and persistence

This notebook demonstrates how AutoDQ workspaces actually behave. It creates
two independent projects under one workspace root, gives each project its own
datasets and analytical artifacts, saves them, switches between them, and
proves that their state does not leak across workspace boundaries.

Run the creation section once. Workspace names are intentionally unique and
cannot be overwritten. On later sessions, skip the two CREATE cells and begin
with one of the OPEN cells in the restoration section.
# %% [markdown] 1. Start from a standalone source dataset

The DATASET declaration initializes the ADQL file. WORKSPACE CREATE then copies
the active source into isolated workspace storage as its `main` dataset.
# %% [Load the sales source]
DATASET '../datasets/sample/sales.csv' TARGET Revenue;
# %% [Inspect existing workspaces]
WORKSPACE LIST ROOT '../workspaces';
# %% [markdown] 2. Create the sales workspace

This is a one-time cell. The workspace gets a normalized identifier, its own
directory tree, a copied primary dataset, target metadata, and a session log.
# %% [Create sales workspace - run once]
WORKSPACE CREATE adql_sales_workspace_demo
    ROOT '../workspaces'
    TARGET Revenue;
# %% [Inspect sales workspace metadata]
WORKSPACE INFO;
# %% [Normalize a persistent data type]
SET TYPE Date datetime FORMAT 'YYYY-MM-DD';
# %% [Register a related dataset]
ADD DATASET customers
    FROM '../datasets/sample/customers.csv';
# %% [Inspect the sales workspace registry]
LIST DATASETS;
# %% [Profile the workspace primary dataset]
PROFILE main;
# %% [Check critical sales fields]
ASSERT "Transaction ID" NOT NULL SEVERITY error FAIL ON never;
ASSERT "Transaction ID" UNIQUE SEVERITY warning FAIL ON never;
ASSERT Revenue MIN 0 SEVERITY error FAIL ON never;
# %% [Clean the active sales dataset]
CLEAN;
# %% [Retain a cleaned workspace dataset]
LET "Sales Clean" = CLEANED OVERWRITE;
# %% [Create a reusable date feature]
FEATURE CREATE "Order Year" METHOD date_year COLUMN Date;
# %% [Create a reusable margin feature]
FEATURE CREATE "Gross Margin"
    METHOD difference
    COLUMNS Revenue,Cost;
# %% [Retain the engineered sales dataset]
LET "Sales Engineered" = ENGINEERED OVERWRITE;
# %% [Create a workspace summary dataset]
LET "Regional Summary" = SELECT Region,
                              COUNT(*) AS transactions,
                              SUM(Revenue) AS "Total Revenue",
                              AVG(Profit) AS "Average Profit"
                       FROM "Sales Engineered"
                       GROUP BY Region
                       ORDER BY "Total Revenue" DESC
                       OVERWRITE;
# %% [Activate the dataset that should reopen later]
USE DATASET "Sales Engineered";
# %% [Inspect the active sales dataset]
HEAD 10;
# %% [markdown] 3. Add governance artifacts to the sales workspace

Contracts and drift baselines live in memory until WORKSPACE SAVE persists
them inside this workspace. They are restored automatically by WORKSPACE OPEN.
# %% [Create a sales schema contract]
CONTRACT workspace_sales_contract FROM "Sales Engineered"
    VERSION 1.0.0
    EXTRA COLUMNS warning
    INFER RANGES false
    INFER CATEGORIES true
    OVERWRITE;
# %% [Require a valid revenue column]
CONTRACT workspace_sales_contract REQUIRE Revenue
    TYPE numeric NOT NULL MIN 0 SEVERITY error;
# %% [Validate the sales contract]
CHECK CONTRACT workspace_sales_contract
    ON "Sales Engineered"
    FAIL ON never;
# %% [Create a sales drift baseline]
BASELINE workspace_sales_baseline
    FROM "Sales Engineered"
    OVERWRITE;
# %% [Verify the baseline against current data]
CHECK DRIFT workspace_sales_baseline
    ON "Sales Engineered"
    CONTRACT workspace_sales_contract
    SENSITIVITY normal
    FAIL ON never;
# %% [markdown] 4. Train state that belongs only to the sales workspace

The model is stored under the workspace models directory when `INCLUDE MODEL`
is true. Opening this workspace with `LOAD MODEL true` restores it for
prediction.
# %% [Train a sales model]
MODEL TARGET Revenue USING decision_tree_regressor
    TEST SIZE 0.20
    RANDOM STATE 42
    USE ENGINEERED false
    EXCLUDE "Transaction ID","Customer ID";
# %% [Generate predictions before persistence]
PREDICT CONFIDENCE 0.90 UNCERTAINTY true;
# %% [Save every persistent sales artifact]
WORKSPACE SAVE
    INCLUDE MODEL true
    MODEL NAME 'revenue_model';
# %% [Confirm saved sales state]
WORKSPACE INFO;
SESSION DATASETS;
# %% [markdown] 5. Create an independent inventory workspace

The inventory source is temporarily registered in the sales session only so it
can become the seed for a new workspace. The last saved sales workspace is not
changed by the cells below.
# %% [Register the inventory seed]
ADD DATASET "Inventory Seed"
    FROM '../datasets/sample/inventory_network.csv';
# %% [Make inventory the active source]
USE DATASET "Inventory Seed";
# %% [Create inventory workspace - run once]
WORKSPACE CREATE adql_inventory_workspace_demo
    ROOT '../workspaces'
    TARGET Backorders;
# %% [Inspect inventory workspace metadata]
WORKSPACE INFO;
# %% [Normalize inventory date]
SET TYPE "Snapshot Date" datetime FORMAT 'YYYY-MM-DD';
# %% [Create inventory value]
FEATURE CREATE "Inventory Value" METHOD expression
    EXPRESSION '`On Hand` * `Unit Cost`';
# %% [Create an operational exception flag]
FEATURE CREATE "Has Backorder" METHOD flag_greater_equal
    COLUMN Backorders
    EXPRESSION '1';
# %% [Retain inventory operational data]
LET "Inventory Operational" = ENGINEERED OVERWRITE;
# %% [Activate inventory operational data]
USE DATASET "Inventory Operational";
# %% [Recognize operational roles]
OPERATIONS DATASET "Inventory Operational"
    ENTITY SKU
    TIME "Snapshot Date"
    STATUS "Has Backorder"
    STAGE Echelon
    DURATION "Lead Time Days"
    COST "Inventory Value"
    QUANTITY "On Hand"
    CAPACITY "Storage Capacity"
    GROUP BY Location,Echelon
    SLA 5
    PERIOD day
    TOP 20;
# %% [Run multi-echelon inventory analysis]
INVENTORY DATASET "Inventory Operational"
    ITEM SKU
    LOCATION Location
    ECHELON Echelon
    PARENT "Parent Location"
    TIME "Snapshot Date"
    ON HAND "On Hand"
    ON ORDER "On Order"
    BACKORDER Backorders
    DEMAND "Daily Demand"
    LEAD TIME "Lead Time Days"
    SAFETY STOCK "Safety Stock"
    UNIT COST "Unit Cost"
    CAPACITY "Storage Capacity"
    SERVICE LEVEL 95
    HORIZON 14
    TOP 20;
# %% [Create an inventory schema contract]
CONTRACT workspace_inventory_contract FROM "Inventory Operational"
    VERSION 1.0.0
    EXTRA COLUMNS warning
    INFER RANGES false
    INFER CATEGORIES true
    OVERWRITE;
# %% [Require non-negative stock]
CONTRACT workspace_inventory_contract REQUIRE "On Hand"
    TYPE numeric NOT NULL MIN 0 SEVERITY error;
# %% [Create an inventory drift baseline]
BASELINE workspace_inventory_baseline
    FROM "Inventory Operational"
    OVERWRITE;
# %% [Create an inventory summary dataset]
LET "Echelon Summary" = SELECT Echelon,
                             COUNT(*) AS "Sku Locations",
                             SUM("On Hand") AS "On Hand",
                             SUM(Backorders) AS backorders,
                             AVG("Lead Time Days") AS "Average Lead Time"
                      FROM "Inventory Operational"
                      GROUP BY Echelon
                      ORDER BY backorders DESC
                      OVERWRITE;
# %% [Save inventory without a model]
WORKSPACE SAVE INCLUDE MODEL false;
# %% [Confirm saved inventory state]
WORKSPACE INFO;
SESSION DATASETS;
# %% [markdown] 6. Compare the persistent workspace inventory

Both workspaces share the same root but retain separate manifests, datasets,
targets, sessions, governance artifacts, models, and generated files.
# %% [List both workspaces]
WORKSPACE LIST ROOT '../workspaces';
# %% [markdown] 7. Restore the sales workspace

Opening replaces the in-memory project with the selected workspace state. The
saved active dataset, target, registered datasets, data types, contracts,
baseline, session, and model are restored together.
# %% [Open sales and restore its model]
WORKSPACE OPEN adql_sales_workspace_demo
    ROOT '../workspaces'
    LOAD MODEL true;
# %% [Verify restored sales metadata]
WORKSPACE INFO;
# %% [Verify restored sales datasets]
LIST DATASETS;
# %% [Verify restored sales governance]
CONTRACT LIST;
BASELINE LIST;
# %% [Use the restored model]
PREDICT CONFIDENCE 0.90 UNCERTAINTY true;
# %% [Inspect the restored sales session]
SESSION;
SESSION EVENTS LIMIT 20;
# %% [markdown] 8. Prove that SAVE is the persistence boundary

This temporary dataset is created after the last sales save. It exists only in
the current in-memory session. Switching away and reopening sales will discard
it because no WORKSPACE SAVE follows this assignment.
# %% [Create an intentionally unsaved dataset]
LET "Session Only Sales Copy" = CURRENT OVERWRITE;
# %% [Show the temporary in-memory dataset]
LIST DATASETS;
# %% [markdown] 9. Switch to inventory and verify isolation

The inventory registry contains its own datasets and no sales datasets. Its
governance definitions are also independent from the sales definitions.
# %% [Open inventory without a model]
WORKSPACE OPEN adql_inventory_workspace_demo
    ROOT '../workspaces'
    LOAD MODEL false;
# %% [Verify restored inventory metadata]
WORKSPACE INFO;
# %% [Verify restored inventory datasets]
LIST DATASETS;
# %% [Verify restored inventory governance]
CONTRACT LIST;
BASELINE LIST;
# %% [Inspect restored inventory data]
HEAD 10;
# %% [Inspect the restored inventory session]
SESSION;
# %% [markdown] 10. Reopen sales and confirm unsaved state was discarded

The restored registry contains the datasets from the last WORKSPACE SAVE, but
`Session Only Sales Copy` is absent. This proves that changing an in-memory
workspace and saving a workspace are separate actions.
# %% [Reopen the saved sales boundary]
WORKSPACE OPEN adql_sales_workspace_demo
    ROOT '../workspaces'
    LOAD MODEL true;
# %% [Confirm only saved sales datasets returned]
LIST DATASETS;
# %% [Confirm the saved model still works]
PREDICT CONFIDENCE 0.90 UNCERTAINTY true;
# %% [Final workspace and session inspection]
WORKSPACE INFO;
WORKSPACE LIST ROOT '../workspaces';
SESSION DATASETS;
# %% [markdown] What this notebook proves

- CREATE establishes isolated storage and copies the active source as `main`.
- Named datasets remain local to the active workspace.
- USE DATASET controls which dataset is active when a workspace is saved.
- SAVE persists datasets, target, dtypes, session, contracts, baselines, audit
  state, and optionally the active model.
- OPEN replaces current memory with the selected saved workspace state.
- `LOAD MODEL` controls whether the saved model is restored.
- Unsaved in-memory changes disappear after switching away.
- LIST and INFO expose workspace inventory and active-workspace metadata.
